{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetWGA3MsP9YLN1g8XmWN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n- `Shipment.kt:9-14`: Shipment model with status field of enum type ShipmentStatus (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- `ShipmentController.kt:1-56`: Current endpoints: POST /shipments (create), GET /shipments/{id}, GET /shipments (list)\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:11-27`: In-memory repository with save, findById, existsById, findAll\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:11-30`: Exception hierarchy with `ResourceNotFoundException` (404), `ConflictException` (409)\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:14-28`: Central exception-to-ApiError mapping\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37`: ErrorCode enum currently has ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt:1-84`: Existing tests for create, getById, list, with error cases\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- Controllers throw ApiExceptions; GlobalExceptionHandler transforms them to ApiError responses\n- Status codes are determined by exception type (409 for ConflictException, 404 for ResourceNotFoundException)\n- ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED) for creation endpoints\n- Error codes are centralized in the ErrorCode enum\n- Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath for assertions\n- Repository methods return plain values or nullable types, controller handles exceptions\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` — Must add new error code for rejecting CANCELLED shipments (e.g., SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE or SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM)\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — Must add POST /{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Must add tests for confirm behavior (4+ test cases)\n\n**Risks:**\n- If the error code name is wrong, existing error handling contract breaks\n- Idempotency requirement (retrying confirm on CONFIRMED succeeds): logic must check current status and only update if CREATED\n- CANCELLED rejection must use ConflictException with appropriate error code\n\n**Open questions:** None — ticket specifies all required behavior clearly.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add error code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to distinguish \"cannot confirm\" from \"already exists\" conflicts. The 409 response will use this code when a CANCELLED shipment is confirmed.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add endpoint:\n   ```\n   @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\n   fun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): ResponseEntity<Shipment>\n   ```\n   Logic:\n   - Query repository for shipment by id → throw ResourceNotFoundException if missing (404)\n   - If status is CREATED: transition to CONFIRMED, save, return 200 with updated shipment\n   - If status is CONFIRMED: return 200 with unchanged shipment (idempotent retry)\n   - If status is CANCELLED: throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE (409)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four test methods:\n   - `confirms a created shipment to CONFIRMED status` — Create S-1, confirm it, verify status changed\n   - `confirm on already confirmed shipment succeeds without change` — Create S-2, confirm twice, verify second call succeeds with status still CONFIRMED\n   - `confirm on cancelled shipment is rejected with 409` — Insert CANCELLED shipment directly, confirm it, verify 409 with error code\n   - `confirm on unknown shipment is rejected with 404` — Confirm non-existent ID, verify 404 with error code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Use a separate \"ConfirmShipmentException\" class instead of ConflictException: Rejected because ConflictException already exists and 409 is the correct HTTP status for state conflicts. The error code (SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE) distinguishes this from other conflict cases.\n- Return 200 OK for CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED, but treat it differently (e.g., 204 No Content): Rejected because idempotent operations typically return the resource, and 200 is the standard response when the operation succeeds. 204 would lose the shipment data in the response.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\nCase 1: Confirm a CREATED shipment\n- Read: Shipment from repository by id\n- Logic: status == CREATED\n- Write: Save updated Shipment with status CONFIRMED\n- Response: 200 OK, Shipment body\n\nCase 2: Confirm an already-CONFIRMED shipment (retry)\n- Read: Shipment from repository by id\n- Logic: status == CONFIRMED\n- Write: None (idempotent)\n- Response: 200 OK, Shipment body unchanged\n\nCase 3: Confirm a CANCELLED shipment\n- Read: Shipment from repository by id\n- Logic: status == CANCELLED\n- Write: None\n- Response: 409 Conflict, ApiError body with code SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n\nCase 4: Confirm unknown shipment\n- Read: Shipment not found\n- Logic: repository returns null\n- Write: None\n- Response: 404 Not Found, ApiError body with code SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n| Test | Setup | Action | Verify |\n|------|-------|--------|--------|\n| confirms CREATED to CONFIRMED | Create S-create | POST /shipments/S-create/confirm | status 200, body.status == CONFIRMED |\n| confirms CONFIRMED idempotently | Create S-retry, confirm once | POST /shipments/S-retry/confirm again | status 200, body.status == CONFIRMED |\n| rejects CANCELLED with 409 | Insert CANCELLED S-cancelled directly | POST /shipments/S-cancelled/confirm | status 409, error.code == SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE |\n| rejects unknown with 404 | (none) | POST /shipments/S-missing/confirm | status 404, error.code == SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND |\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":739,"cache_read_input_tokens":16818,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":739},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics"